<%# The record button (docs/VOICE_CAPTURE.md): studio/voice_recorder opens the
    microphone through studio/microphone (so it records from what the chip
    names), runs the engine's one level meter (studio/level_meter) as the ring
    around the button, refuses a silent take, and hands a heard take to the page
    as a studio:voice-recorder:take event with the blob. It uploads nothing:
    the page that renders it decides where the audio goes.

    Locals, all optional:
      copy:   per-state words merged over studio/voice_recorder's COPY
              (e.g. { "idle" => { "button" => "Talk" } })
      mode:   "toggle" (tap to start, tap to stop; the default) or "hold"
              (press and hold to talk)
      max_ms: stop a take on its own after this long (default 60000)
      id:     an id for the root, for a page's own listener

    The controller is lazy (studio/stimulus); if it fails to load, the root
    carries data-studio-controller-failed="voice-recorder" and says so. %>
<% copy = Studio::VoiceCapture.recorder_copy(local_assigns[:copy]) %>
<% mode = local_assigns.fetch(:mode, "toggle").to_s == "hold" ? "hold" : "toggle" %>
<%= render "studio/voice/styles" %>
<div class="studio-recorder"
     <%= tag.attributes(id: local_assigns[:id]) %>
     data-studio-controller="voice-recorder"
     data-voice-recorder-state="idle"
     data-voice-recorder-mode="<%= mode %>"
     data-voice-recorder-max-ms="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:max_ms, 60_000).to_i %>"
     data-voice-recorder-copy="<%= copy.except("unavailable").to_json %>">
  <button type="button" class="studio-recorder-button" data-voice-recorder-button aria-pressed="false">
    <span data-voice-recorder-label><%= copy.dig("idle", "button") %></span>
  </button>
  <span class="studio-recorder-timer" data-voice-recorder-timer aria-hidden="true">0:00</span>
  <p class="studio-recorder-status" data-voice-recorder-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="studio-recorder-failed"><%= copy["unavailable"] %></p>
</div>
